#X obj 645 8 flow.speedlim;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 210 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object passes through all control data no more often
than the specified limit in milliseconds \, and drops all messages
that arrive within that interval;
#X text 240 138 initially the object is open \, on the first message
it passes it and then becomes closed for the specified time interval
\, after which it goes back to the open state;
#X text 240 193 @limit sets the time limit \, a value of 0 means no
limitations;
#X text 240 218 the object can be used for button debouncing or to
throttle a stream of control messages \, for example to limit the rate
of a slider output;
